{
  "$comment": [
    "MCP servers for the dev3d office.",
    "",
    "Copy this file to `mcp.json` (or point DEV3D_MCP_CONFIG at it) and edit the",
    "servers you want. Nothing here is enabled until a server is listed, so an",
    "absent mcp.json means no MCP at all.",
    "",
    "Every server's tools are published to employees as mcp__<id>__<tool>, so the",
    "`id` you choose is part of the name a role is granted. Two servers may both",
    "offer a tool called `search` without colliding.",
    "",
    "Which roles may call these tools is DEV3D_MCP_GRANT_ROLES (default: the roles",
    "that already hold run_shell). A remote server can be a filesystem, a database",
    "or a deployment system, so tools are granted deliberately and never inherited."
  ],
  "servers": [
    {
      "id": "fs",
      "description": "Read and write files through the reference filesystem server.",
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem", "."],
      "enabled": false
    },
    {
      "id": "git",
      "description": "Repository history and diffs, over MCP.",
      "command": "uvx",
      "args": ["mcp-server-git", "--repository", "."],
      "enabled": false
    },
    {
      "id": "memory",
      "description": "A knowledge graph the office can write notes into.",
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory"],
      "enabled": false
    },
    {
      "id": "remote",
      "description": "A hosted MCP server over Streamable HTTP. Headers are sent verbatim: no ${VAR} interpolation happens here, so keep a secret in a file this repository ignores, or set DEV3D_MCP_SERVERS for a local server instead.",
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.example.com/mcp",
      "headers": { "authorization": "Bearer paste-your-token-here" },
      "enabled": false
    }
  ]
}
